      "record_id": "23570763",
      "native_and_scholarly_identity_and_private_gates": {
        "title": "A symmetric ideal chain with periodic Lefschetz behavior in positive characteristic",
        "description": "One fixed two-row symmetric ideal chain has periodic weak and strong Lefschetz behavior in positive characteristic, with a classification over every field extension.",
        "abstract": "For each fixed field of positive characteristic p, we construct a single compatible symmetric chain of Artinian ideals in two rows of variables, generated from width three. At every width n ≥ 2, its quotient has both the weak and strong Lefschetz properties exactly when p ∤ n − 1. The quadratic quotient is free over the integers, and a determinant for an arbitrary linear form gives the classification over every field extension. In particular, over the fixed infinite field 𝔽ₚ(t) both properties hold and fail at unbounded widths. This gives a negative answer to the unrestricted eventual dichotomies posed by Römer. It gives no negative answer in characteristic zero or in one row.",
        "author": "Alec Kriebel",
        "orcid": "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-9320-500X",
        "publication_date": "2026-10-22",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "printed_version": "1.0.0",
